---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { BOOKING_URL } from '../data/site';
import portrait from '../assets/tanya-headshot.webp';
---

<Base title="About" description="About the practitioner — an Associate Clinical Social Worker offering EMDR, somatic, and nature-based therapy in California.">

  <article class="about container-narrow section">
    <header class="about-header">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>Therapy that meets you where you are.</h1>
    </header>

    <figure class="portrait">
      <Image
        src={portrait}
        alt="Tanya L. Hauer"
        class="portrait-img"
        widths={[360, 540, 720]}
        sizes="(min-width: 640px) 360px, 80vw"
        format="webp"
        loading="eager"
      />
    </figure>

    <section class="prose">
      <p class="lede">
        I believe healing doesn't have to happen in a sterile office under
        fluorescent lights. Some of the most meaningful shifts happen when you
        feel grounded, safe, and connected — to your body, your environment,
        and yourself.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="prose">
      <h2>Background</h2>
      <p>
        I'm an Associate Clinical Social Worker, and my work is rooted in
        understanding how the nervous system holds and processes experience.
        When something overwhelming happens, it doesn't just live in your
        thoughts — it lives in your body.
      </p>
      <p>
        I integrate clinical training with embodied, experiential healing —
        blending trauma-informed care with EMDR, somatic therapy, sound, and
        nature-based practices. These methods help you move through what's
        stuck, rather than just talk about it. I believe healing happens in
        relationship, safety, and attunement — not urgency.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="prose">
      <h2>How I work</h2>
      <p>
        I work in a way that is steady, collaborative, and attuned. You don't
        have to perform, explain everything perfectly, or have it all figured
        out.
      </p>
      <p>
        We go at a pace that feels safe for your system — building capacity,
        not pushing past your limits.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="prose closing">
      <p>
        Healing is not about becoming someone new.
        <br />
        It's about coming back to yourself.
      </p>
    </section>

    <aside class="credentials" aria-labelledby="credentials-heading">
      <h2 id="credentials-heading" class="eyebrow">Credentials &amp; supervision</h2>
      <p>
        Tanya L. Hauer, MSW, ACSW #134498
        <br />
        Associate Clinical Social Worker, registered with the California Board
        of Behavioral Sciences
        <br />
        Supervised by Celynna Harnetiaux, LMFT #118714
      </p>
    </aside>

    <div class="cta-row">
      <a
        href={BOOKING_URL}
        class="btn btn-primary"
        data-cta="book-consult"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >
        Book a Consult
      </a>
    </div>
  </article>

</Base>

<style>
  .about-header { margin-bottom: var(--space-lg); }
  .about-header .eyebrow { margin-bottom: var(--space-2xs); }

  .portrait {
    margin: 0 auto var(--space-lg);
    max-width: 360px;
  }
  .portrait-img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  }

  .prose { margin-bottom: var(--space-lg); }
  .prose h2 {
    font-size: var(--fs-h3);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2xs);
  }

  .prose.closing p {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: var(--fs-h3);
    line-height: var(--lh-snug);
    color: var(--color-sage-deep);
  }

  .credentials {
    margin-block: var(--space-xl);
    padding: var(--space-md);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    background: var(--color-sage-light);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .credentials .eyebrow { margin-bottom: var(--space-2xs); }

  .cta-row { margin-top: var(--space-lg); }
</style>
